# Docs page header

Shared chrome for every docs entry. Do **not** invent a bespoke page header.

Canonical implementation:

- [`components/docs/docs-page-header.tsx`](components/docs/docs-page-header.tsx) — breadcrumb, Copy page, Prev/Next, title, one-line intro, single layer/kind badge
- [`components/docs/render-component-docs.tsx`](components/docs/render-component-docs.tsx) — Preview (demo only) + separate Usage peek + compact install; no shared border frame
- [`components/docs/docs-table-of-contents.tsx`](components/docs/docs-table-of-contents.tsx) — right-rail “On this page”
- Frozen anatomy still applies: [`docs/page-anatomy.md`](docs/page-anatomy.md)

## First fold (required order)

1. Breadcrumb (`Home / {group}`) + Copy page + Prev/Next (sidebar order)
2. Title + one-sentence `entry.description` + **one** badge (`Data-aware` | `Primitive` | `Map` | `Tool` | `Block` | `Draft` | `Coming soon`)
3. Optional reserved slot for a variant switcher — **do not build until a page needs it**
4. **Preview** — live demo only. No outer border/card from `renderComponentDocs`. Demos may use their own single border if needed; never wrap again.
5. **Usage** — code peek (3 lines + View code) as its **own** section under Preview, not nested inside a Preview frame
6. Compact “Copy install command”, then full Installation tabs below the fold when `registryUrl` is set
7. MDX / body sections per page-anatomy
8. Composition (`builtWith` / `usesFoundations` / `usedBy`) **exactly once** in the body — never in the hero

## Borders

- Prefer **no** chrome border around Preview.
- At most **one** border on a demo surface (owned by the demo, e.g. line-strip cards).
- Never wrap demo + code in a shared bordered frame (double wrapping).
- Code uses the syntax block’s own muted surface only.

## Rules for new components

1. Every new docs entry goes through `DocsPageHeader` (or `renderComponentDocs` / `ComingSoonDocsPage` / `SectionHub` which already use it). Never a custom `<h1>` stack.
2. Keep `description` to **one sentence**. Detail belongs in MDX.
3. Data-aware / primitive pages should register a short usage snippet in `PREVIEW_SNIPPETS` (or pass `getDataExample`) so the Preview peek has content. If omitted, the peek panel is skipped.
4. Do **not** put get-data boxes, install tabs, or relationship badges in the hero.
5. Do **not** stack group + layer + “Installable” badges — `entryBadgeLabel` is the only badge.
6. Layers stay distinct: shared chrome does not collapse Interface / Primitive / Foundation / Map / Block / Tool into one shadcn-style template. Body sections still follow [`docs/page-anatomy.md`](docs/page-anatomy.md).
7. Headings that should appear in the TOC must have stable `id`s (MDX headings already do via `mdx-components.tsx`; hand-coded `h2`/`h3` must set `id` too).

## Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom header with badge pile + get-data in hero
<header>
  <Badge>Data-aware</Badge>
  <Badge>Data-aware</Badge>
  <Badge>Installable</Badge>
  <h1>…</h1>
  <RelationshipBadges … />
  <pre>{/* full get-data snippet */}</pre>
</header>

// ✅ GOOD — DocsPageHeader; Preview and Usage are separate, no outer frame
<>
  <DocsPageHeader entry={entry} />
  {/* Preview = demo only; Usage = code peek; no shared border wrapper */}
</>
```
